uger CLI and the exposed\nsurface can drift and how that is checked — auger's argv surface is the product today, so a spec\nthat describes a surface nobody tests against the CLI is the drift risk to design out.\n\n             DELIVERABLE — the contract and the wiring, frozen on this row:\n             1. the OpenAPI 3.x document muster will be pointed at (file or served route), with its\n                location named precisely and its generation rule stated (hand-written vs generated\n                from the route table — this repo's own doctrine decides which)\n             2. operationIds, request/response schemas, and the servers[] url that muster dereferences\n                (muster falls back to the spec's own servers[].url when --base-url is omitted; a\n                RELATIVE servers url cannot be dereferenced standalone — say which case applies)\n             3. the consumer config block + a three-line human quickstart (the CLI form:\n                openapi-cli <generated-verb>), both added to this repo's docs\n             4. the parity rule: what keeps the spec from drifting off the real routes, in the\n                same shape as this repo's existing drift checks\n\n             ACCEPTANCE: the spec parses in muster's own parser, the consumer block is copy-pasteable,\n             and the parity rule is expressed as an executable check (not a comment).", "capability_tags": ["+integration", "+protocol", "+interop"], "attempts": 0, "blocked_reason": null, "blocked_since": null, "blocks": [], "ci_result": null, "commit_hash": null, "completed_at": null, "depends_on": ["AUG-065"], "dispatched_at": null, "exit_code": null, "fallback_model": null, "fallback_provider": null, "files_changed": [], "foreman_note": null, "guard_result": null, "perpetual": null, "primary_model": null, "primary_provider": null, "review_notes": null, "worker_status": "pending", "worker_summary": null, "detail": {"fingerprint": "ab680d81435f3c2296e52e5459c5e8baa4a792af225db2f940